      "title": "Indirect heating through jacket and paddles",
      "description": "Steam (or thermal oil) heats the trough jacket and the inside of the hollow shafts and paddles, so the heating surface per unit volume is very large. The material never touches the heating medium, and only a small vapour stream leaves — easy to condense or treat. Used for sludges, pastes and filter cakes.",
